--  CuBit
--  Copyright (C) 2026 Jon Andrew
--
--  @summary
--  The Utah teapot: Martin Newell's 1975 bicubic Bezier control points
--  (public domain), as published in Frank Crow, "The Origins of the
--  Teapot", IEEE CG&A 7(1), 1987. Z is up. Newell defined one quadrant or
--  half of each piece and the rest by symmetry: the first six patches
--  (rim, body, lid, bottom) repeat in four quadrants rotated about Z, the
--  last four (handle, spout) are mirrored across Y = 0. 32 patches in all.
--  The bottom patch is the later addition every distributed teaset carries.
--  These are control points, not a mesh: Teapot_Mesh tessellates them when
--  the gallery starts. tests/gpu-canvas cross-checks the values against
--  FreeGLUT's copy (tests/mesa-teapot/teapot-control-points.h), which adds
--  two 0.002 offsets at the lid apex that Newell's single point does not.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
